@page "/about"
@using GardenPlotWeb.Services
@using GardenPlotWeb.Services.Persistence
@inject IPlantProfileService PlantProfiles

<PageTitle>About Garden Plot</PageTitle>

<h1>About Garden Plot</h1>

<p class="text-muted">Keyboard controls report and recommendations.</p>

<h2>Licensing and community</h2>
<p>
    Garden Plot is built to support home growers, hobbyists, and learners.
    If you are planning your own personal garden, you are welcome to use Garden Plot at no cost.
</p>
<p>
    If you are using Garden Plot for commercial work (for example, paid landscape design, garden consulting,
    or other client-facing professional services), a commercial account and license are required.
</p>
<p>
    We want active feedback from landscape architects and related professionals so we can shape the product with the community.
    As an early-adopter program, the first 10 companies that engage with us will be offered a one-year commercial license for $1.
    We are also exploring a Patreon-based model where an active Patreon membership may include commercial-use access.
</p>

<h2>Current keyboard controls</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Enter</strong> in zoom textbox: apply typed zoom.</li>
    <li><strong>Shift/Ctrl/Alt + Mouse wheel</strong>: selection/item rotation and group orientation workflows.</li>
    <li><strong>Stamp line/array mode:</strong> Arrow keys adjust spacing (X; Y for arrays).</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+Z</strong>: undo.</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+A</strong>: select all.</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+C</strong>: copy selection.</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl+V</strong>: paste.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete / Backspace</strong>: delete selected items.</li>
    <li><strong>[</strong> / <strong>]</strong>: rotate selection or active stamp.</li>
    <li><strong>Escape</strong>: cancel current draft/preview and return to Select.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data sources &amp; attribution</h2>
<p>
    Plant profile data in Garden Plot is curated and merged from the following public sources by the
    <code>GardenPlot.DataFetcher</code> tool. Every <em>PlantProfile</em> records the sources it pulled from,
    surfaced inline in the info panel.
</p>

@{
    string? lastRefresh = (PlantProfiles as LocalPlantProfileService)?.DataVersion?.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd");
}
<p class="text-muted small">
    Last plant-data refresh: <strong>@(lastRefresh ?? "unknown")</strong> (rebuild and re-run the data fetcher to update).
</p>

<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Source</th>
            <th>Used for</th>
            <th>License</th>
            <th>Attribution</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>
                <a href="https://plants.usda.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USDA PLANTS Database</a>
            </td>
            <td>Accepted scientific name, family/genus, common name, U.S. and territory native/introduced status.</td>
            <td>U.S. Government work — Public Domain (17 U.S.C. § 105).</td>
            <td>Courtesy credit; no attribution required.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>
                <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikidata</a>
            </td>
            <td>Cross-reference IDs, family/genus, common names (multilingual), native range hints, Wikipedia links.</td>
            <td>
                <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC0 1.0</a>
                for structured data.
            </td>
            <td>"Wikidata contributors" (requested).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>
                <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>
            </td>
            <td>Live summary excerpts shown in the selection info panel.</td>
            <td>
                <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.
                Excerpts are fetched live and not redistributed by Garden Plot itself.
            </td>
            <td>"Wikipedia contributors", with link back to the source article.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>
                <a href="https://www.aspca.org/pet-care/animal-poison-control/toxic-and-non-toxic-plants" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASPCA toxic plant list</a>
            </td>
            <td>Hand-curated pet-toxicity notes (cat/dog/human severity).</td>
            <td>Factual material from a public reference. Garden Plot does not republish ASPCA prose.</td>
            <td>Reference link included on individual entries where applicable.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p class="small">
    Fetch policy: Garden Plot ships pre-merged data in <code>wwwroot/data/plant-profiles.json</code> so the
    running app makes no outbound calls for built-in palette items. The fetcher uses a real
    <code>User-Agent</code>, ETag-based conditional requests, and bounded concurrency to minimise
    bandwidth on upstream providers.
</p>

<hr />
<p class="text-muted small mb-0">
    Plot data schema: <strong>v@PlotSchema.Current</strong>
</p>
